  "scope": "The literal10180-slot program traverses the original binary loop budget, executes each actual minimum-selected full packing guess, retains its complete optional state, increments the actual exponent word and decrements the actual remaining word. Its recursive call returns into the tail register while retaining the original head state, then allocates the ordered list. Every head executes even when its inner packing has stopped. The universal trace supports arbitrary incoming return destinations. The returned list equals the original guessesFrom state fields when minimumPositive selects an index; empty/all-zero rows have explicit optional-output behavior, and length is the original numerical fuel value. No updated words, guess outcome, tail list or intermediate packing state is supplied. The same actual physical run preserves original context/words/source and pays halt. Its recursive instruction envelope uses original rows/demand count/exponent/fuel; numerical dependence remains explicit. Original context representation, initial H/B, dense cursor and the original exponent/fuel words remain premises. Context/grid-budget construction, a derived grid-range polynomial envelope, old operation-counter equality and final dispatch remain separate. Twelve physical cases and three separately labelled natural-reference comparisons independently check literal list order, full raw state fields/events, counter carry and padded words."
}
